{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/AI for Climate Action.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/AI for Climate Action.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"ai for climate action ai for climate action","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/AI for Climate Action.md","fileName":"AI for Climate Action.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"AI for Climate Action","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 23:09\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[AI Labor and Environmental Ethics]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["AI Labor and Environmental Ethics","AI Energy Consumption","aiethics.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/AI for Climate Action.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/AI for Climate Action.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"ai for climate action ai for climate action","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/AI for Climate Action.md","fileName":"AI for Climate Action.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"AI for Climate Action","heading":"AI for Climate Action","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"AI for climate action applies pattern recognition, modeling, monitoring, and coordination to environmental problems. Systems can analyze complex environmental data, improve energy management, support smart grids or agriculture, and help implement reductions in harmful emissions.\n\nThese capabilities make AI a tool rather than a complete climate policy. Models do not decide how costs should be distributed, which goals deserve priority, or how conflicts among communities and nonhuman interests should be resolved. The environmental benefit must also be compared with [[AI Energy Consumption]] and material infrastructure. Useful computation complements political action and practical wisdom instead of replacing them.","tags":["baby"],"links":["AI Labor and Environmental Ethics","AI Energy Consump